00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:45.240
- [Eric] Eight kilometers of walkways.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.463
- [Johnny] Eight kilometers?
- [Eric] Yeah.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:49.860
- Oh, and with the most gnarly doors

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:51.210
you've ever seen in your life.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:55.350
They're quadruple fortified
with huge slabs of concrete.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:57.603
- This is like two meters of concrete.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.390
It sit behind there with a rifle

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:02.100
and be able to protect the entrances.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:06.303
- Wow. No one is getting into
this bunker anytime soon.

00:02:09.841 --> 00:02:12.180
(gentle plucky music)

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:14.790
I went to Switzerland to hunt for bunkers.

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:17.730
Fortresses drilled impossibly
deep into mountains

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:20.460
and cliffs and villages hidden from view,

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:22.293
but packing deadly power.

00:02:22.293 --> 00:02:25.320
Oh, wow. I've seen so many bunkers.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:27.270
You don't have to look
super hard to find them.

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:28.590
They're everywhere.

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:30.423
There's a bunker right here, look at this.

00:02:30.423 --> 00:02:31.769
This is not a rock.

00:02:31.769 --> 00:02:33.320
(metal clanking)
This is a door.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:34.650
(birds tweeting)

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:37.800
These little doors in
the middle of the forest,

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:40.470
so unassuming, so benign,

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:42.570
but boy, if you knew what was inside.

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:44.730
Let's be clear, this isn't normal.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.920
Most countries don't bore into mountains

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:48.750
as their defense strategy,

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.880
but Switzerland isn't
like other countries.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.260
- When you live in Switzerland,

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.510
you never really have a sense of threat.

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:56.700
We're Switzerland, we're neutral, right?

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:58.233
Nothing gonna happen to us.

00:02:58.233 --> 00:02:59.340
(ominous music)

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:01.080
- So instead of forming alliances

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.970
and sending troops they dug.

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:06.150
And the results are nearly 10,000 of these

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:08.070
scattered all throughout the country.

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:11.049
And that is what I have
been searching for.

00:03:11.049 --> 00:03:11.882
(drone whirring)

00:03:11.882 --> 00:03:12.715
Okay, okay, okay.

00:03:12.715 --> 00:03:15.150
Where are you, my bunkers?
Where are you, my bunkers?

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:17.010
Ah, I see something down there.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:19.650
That is not natural erosion on this cliff.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:22.590
I keep looking for more
and more and I'm realizing,

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.210
there are too many for me to fly to.

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:25.950
Like, there are dozens up there.

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:29.010
This cliff is just riddled
with little windows,

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.150
totally primed and prepped

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:32.550
to just light up this entire valley

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:35.610
