00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:47.010
That bridge has been used for a long time

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:49.860
to let people flow throughout this pass,

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:52.080
but if you're Switzerland in 1942,

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:53.640
these gateways through the Alps

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:56.370
that have been used for
trade are now a liability.

00:11:56.370 --> 00:11:58.230
They're now a gateway for invading armies

00:11:58.230 --> 00:11:59.850
to come take over your country.

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:04.140
(motorcycle engine revving)
(indistinct chattering)

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:06.000
So this is where they
focus their attention.

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:07.410
All these choke points,

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:10.080
all of these gateways to their mountains.

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:12.900
The idea was if the Italians
start coming from that way

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:15.030
or the Germans start coming from that way

00:12:15.030 --> 00:12:17.160
they can sit in their bunkers

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:20.430
and blow the smithereens out
of anyone coming up this pass.

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:21.870
Because again, it's a choke point.

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:22.980
No one can go anywhere else.

00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:23.910
You can't go over the mountains.

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:25.997
You have to go through this pass.

00:12:25.997 --> 00:12:28.580
(gentle music)

00:12:30.889 --> 00:12:32.530
(dramatic techno music)

00:12:32.530 --> 00:12:34.170
(car engine revving)

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:36.120
All right, I'm down from the
mountains for a little bit

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:39.660
and it's because I got invited
to hang out with this guy.

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:42.210
He's a retired Swiss historian

00:12:42.210 --> 00:12:45.090
who's freaking obsessed
with maps of Switzerland.

00:12:45.090 --> 00:12:47.010
I've never felt so seen in my life.

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:49.410
- I'm a an artillery gunner.

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:52.181
I did my basic training in a fortress.

00:12:52.181 --> 00:12:55.440
And then we went here just for training.

00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:57.630
Zurich in the pre Alps.

00:12:57.630 --> 00:13:01.170
- He's showing me with
this amazing 3D relief map

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:03.630
what this fortress actually looked like.

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:06.240
- Here in these high mountains,

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:10.950
were several very very
important fortresses.

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:15.950
Some here, there were old
ones and some modern new ones.

00:13:16.590 --> 00:13:20.280
Here, here, and even here.

00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:24.330
Here there are bankers
and there is Toblerone.

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:26.070
Do you understand?
- Yes. I saw the Toblerone

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:26.903
on the summer the Southern-
- Toblerone.

00:13:26.903 --> 00:13:31.170
There is a last Toblerone
and also here is one.

00:13:31.170 --> 00:13:35.090
When France was defeated
in the summer 1940,

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:38.250
Switzerland was surrounded by the axis.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:43.110
This was let's say, an emergency solution.

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:44.948
This was to redoubt.

00:13:44.948 --> 00:13:48.281
(gentle ominous music)

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:52.620
- Okay, so I hike up to this Swiss house

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:55.530
in the middle of the Pass.

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:58.200
Looks like just a normal
Swiss house, is beautiful,

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:00.750
but you look closely
and you see something.

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:04.290
These windows aren't real
windows they're painted on.

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:08.250
This thing is actually solid concrete.

00:14:08.250 --> 00:14:09.540
This is not a chalet.

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:11.740
These are not like barn doors.

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:13.799
Oh wait, are they gonna let me do this?

00:14:13.799 --> 00:14:15.299
Oh my God. Oh my (laughs) God.

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:19.230
Look at this.

00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:21.330
Those are just little gun holes.

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:23.609
Put your gun through that
thing and you can shoot.

00:14:23.609 --> 00:14:27.420
(laughs) Oh wow, look at that.

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:30.540
This house is not just a house
with some gun holes in it.

00:14:30.540 --> 00:14:32.733
It's actually a network of tunnels.

00:14:34.590 --> 00:14:35.423
Hey, check this out.

00:14:35.423 --> 00:14:37.405
I found a fake rock with a gun in it.

00:14:37.405 --> 00:14:38.238
(Johnny laughs)

00:14:38.238 --> 00:14:40.200
I was looking at this rock
and it looked a little weird,

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:41.400
a little off up close.

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:42.780
It looks like a real rock.

00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:43.890
It's not.

00:14:43.890 --> 00:14:44.723
Look under.

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:49.683
Yep. Oh yeah.

00:14:50.670 --> 00:14:52.710
Boom, I see your secrets.

00:14:52.710 --> 00:14:55.950
I've looked at enough bunkers
to know what the playbook is.

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:59.640
Hide something either in a
village or in a mountain.

00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:01.890
Put a huge network of tunnels under it

00:15:01.890 --> 00:15:04.440
and just point at the Pass
(guns firing)

00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:07.978
and get ready to fire in
case there's an invasion.

00:15:07.978 --> 00:15:11.311
(gentle ominous music)

00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:15.120
But wait a minute, let's
examine the logic here.

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:16.980
Yeah, it's really cool to have mountains

00:15:16.980 --> 00:15:19.650
full of really protective
bunkers, really cool,

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:22.290
but most people in Switzerland
do not live in the mountains.

00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:25.140
Most people live up here
on this flat plateau

00:15:25.140 --> 00:15:28.290
and in their early 1940s,
they were sitting ducks.

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:32.220
The point here was not to
protect the people directly

00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:34.740
but rather to signal
to Hitler and Mussolini

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:36.990
that if they wanted to
connect their two empires

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:38.490
they would have to go through the Alps

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:40.800
and that that would be incredibly costly

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:42.240
and basically impossible.

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:45.360
It's like using defense as the deterrent.

00:15:45.360 --> 00:15:46.500
Oh, and it worked.

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:49.200
The Nazis had a plan all fleshed
out to invade Switzerland

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:50.190
but they never did it.

00:15:50.190 --> 00:15:52.710
And yes, that is not just
because of these bunkers.

00:15:52.710 --> 00:15:56.460
It is because Switzerland was
letting the Nazis store money

00:15:56.460 --> 00:15:58.230
and stolen stuff in their banks,

00:15:58.230 --> 00:16:00.000
trading with them et cetera.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.430
The bunkers were a part
of the deterrent strategy,

00:16:02.430 --> 00:16:04.110
but the Swiss really paned to the Nazis

00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:06.270
as another form of staying neutral,

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:09.256
something they hear a lot
about even 70 years later.

00:16:09.256 --> 00:16:10.800
(gentle music)

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:13.270
I'm at a dam and if my intel is right

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:19.220
that big giant mountain behind
me is actually a bunker.

00:16:19.702 --> 00:16:21.478
(drone whirring)

00:16:21.478 --> 00:16:22.311
And away.

00:16:23.385 --> 00:16:26.135
(dramatic music)

00:16:27.362 --> 00:16:29.820
I don't see anything.

00:16:29.820 --> 00:16:31.410
Wait a minute, yes I do.

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:32.760
What is that? What is that?

00:16:35.950 --> 00:16:38.010
I see you big boy.

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:42.900
You are a very well hidden gun.

00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:46.020
Wow. That thing blends in very nicely.

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:48.423
With that as their fortress,

00:16:49.981 --> 00:16:51.507
no one can fire back.

00:16:51.507 --> 00:16:54.257
(dramatic music)

00:16:55.290 --> 00:16:58.170
Another hidden bunker, another
successful drone flight.

00:16:58.170 --> 00:16:59.580
Nice job drone.

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:00.810
Let's get outta here.

00:17:00.810 --> 00:17:02.558
Onto the next one.

00:17:02.558 --> 00:17:05.010
(bright twinkly music)

00:17:05.010 --> 00:17:06.600
I hear there's a tunnel up there

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:08.070
at the top of that mountain,

00:17:08.070 --> 00:17:09.993
that foggy, foggy, wet mountain.

00:17:11.370 --> 00:17:12.770
Three and a half kilometers.

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:15.497
I can do this. Let's go.

00:17:15.497 --> 00:17:18.747
(bright twinkly music)

00:17:21.960 --> 00:17:24.180
By the way, big thanks to the subscriber

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:27.990
who recommended this bunker to me.

00:17:27.990 --> 00:17:31.290
I put a call out to ask Swiss people

00:17:31.290 --> 00:17:33.480
what bunkers I should go hunting for,

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:34.970
and this is one of them.

00:17:34.970 --> 00:17:38.220
(bright twinkly music)

00:17:44.569 --> 00:17:47.499
(Johnny exhales sharply)

00:17:47.499 --> 00:17:48.641
(bright twinkly music)

00:17:48.641 --> 00:17:49.474
Wow.

00:17:51.518 --> 00:17:54.410
(gentle suspenseful music)

00:17:54.410 --> 00:17:55.830
So yeah, Hitler never invaded,

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:57.630
Switzerland stayed neutral in the war,

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:59.257
but eventually the Swiss
government was like,

00:17:59.257 --> 00:18:00.817
"Why are we paying for a bunch of bunkers

00:18:00.817 --> 00:18:02.730
"that we designed for Hitler?"

00:18:02.730 --> 00:18:04.541
So they decided to decommission them.

00:18:04.541 --> 00:18:06.630
(gentle suspenseful music)

00:18:06.630 --> 00:18:08.430
A lot of them are totally abandoned,

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:11.250
but then you have private buyers,

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:12.360
people who have bought them

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:14.160
to turn them into whatever they want.

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:15.600
A lot of these are museums

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:18.240
or are owned by like
military organizations

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:19.470
that wanna preserve the history,

00:18:19.470 --> 00:18:21.720
but some people get really
creative with these bunkers.

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:22.950
Like people are growing mushrooms

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:24.510
and fermenting cheese in them,

00:18:24.510 --> 00:18:28.191
or perhaps my favorite use
the place I slept last night.

00:18:28.191 --> 00:18:29.490
(gentle music)

00:18:29.490 --> 00:18:31.222
This is my hotel tonight.

00:18:31.222 --> 00:18:32.940
(gentle music)

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:34.620
I booked this hotel

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:36.840
because I'm making a story about bunkers.

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:38.850
And so I was like, "I have
to stay in a bunker hotel."

00:18:38.850 --> 00:18:42.360
I had no idea it was gonna be this.

00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:45.900
This is a full blown deep
in the mountain bunker.

00:18:45.900 --> 00:18:48.000
There's dripping water everywhere.

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:50.340
Original ladders.

00:18:50.340 --> 00:18:52.164
This place is nuts.

00:18:52.164 --> 00:18:54.747
(gentle music)

00:18:55.858 --> 00:18:59.790
Okay, I guess I'm gonna go
get dinner in this bunker.

00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:02.070
There's a restaurant in it.

00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:03.704
I'm going there now.

00:19:03.704 --> 00:19:06.287
(gentle music)

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:12.464
What is happening?

00:19:12.464 --> 00:19:15.047
(gentle music)

00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:18.540
- [Announcer] Switzerland is
one of the beautiful countries

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:19.373
in the world.

00:19:19.373 --> 00:19:22.170
This small countries
surrounded by powerful nations

00:19:22.170 --> 00:19:25.626
has been able to remain
neutral for the past 150 years.

00:19:25.626 --> 00:19:27.744
150 years, 150 years.

00:19:27.744 --> 00:19:31.200
(bright twinkly music)

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:32.790
- And I'm back in the city

00:19:32.790 --> 00:19:34.950
and I need to tell you
the next part of the story

00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:39.240
because this is where it
becomes relevant to today.

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:40.800
- [Announcer] The Swiss
people have always been ready

00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:42.480
to protect their country.

00:19:42.480 --> 00:19:45.090
- After the bunker digging
strategy worked in World War II

00:19:45.090 --> 00:19:46.470
to keep Switzerland neutral,

00:19:46.470 --> 00:19:48.510
they kind of latched onto the idea,

00:19:48.510 --> 00:19:52.440
digging bunkers worked and they
weren't gonna stop doing it

00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:54.720
but the Nazi threat went away

00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:57.300
and was replaced with a new threat.

00:19:57.300 --> 00:20:00.090
One that would not be deterred by

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:02.737
turning your mountains
into a giant fortress

00:20:02.737 --> 00:20:03.570
(bright twinkly music)

00:20:03.570 --> 00:20:05.850
(military air raid sirens)

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:06.810
- [Announcer] That signal means

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:08.640
to stop whatever you are doing

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:11.100
and get to the nearest safe place fast.

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:14.130
- [Announcer] It is called a
Cold War because armed forces,

00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:16.650
although used as a threat,
are rarely unleashed.

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:19.440
- While the rest of the world
was busy making alliances

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:21.060
and arming themselves,

00:20:21.060 --> 00:20:25.860
the Swiss turned to their
good old strategy of digging,

00:20:25.860 --> 00:20:28.080
but instead of focusing on the mountains

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:29.430
they turned to the city.

00:20:29.430 --> 00:20:31.170
I've been hanging out with Robin,

00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:34.320
a Swiss journalist who's
been showing me around

00:20:34.320 --> 00:20:36.763
the non-mountain version of Swiss bunkers.

00:20:36.763 --> 00:20:39.780
- So this is like a normal basement

00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:42.780
usually in a Swiss house.

00:20:42.780 --> 00:20:47.670
And then behind here you
mostly have this thick door,

00:20:47.670 --> 00:20:51.090
is really nothing special,
it's just a regular seller.

00:20:51.090 --> 00:20:55.470
What we do as Swiss people,
we store golf clubs,

00:20:55.470 --> 00:21:00.470
we store skis, wine, but of
course with a special window,

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:04.530
with a special filter.

00:21:04.530 --> 00:21:06.240
So we close this.

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:07.726
- [Johnny] Oh my gosh.

00:21:07.726 --> 00:21:09.117
- Yep. Like this.

00:21:09.117 --> 00:21:11.310
- [Johnny] Yep. Wow.

00:21:11.310 --> 00:21:14.040
- And then like this.

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:17.310
- It's gotta be funny that
American comes to town

00:21:17.310 --> 00:21:19.230
and is like, "Look at these bunkers."

00:21:19.230 --> 00:21:20.063
And you're just like-

00:21:20.063 --> 00:21:21.718
- "No Johnny, it's just a seller."

00:21:21.718 --> 00:21:22.650
(both laughing)
- It's a seller.

00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:23.775
There's nothing special.

00:21:23.775 --> 00:21:25.530
And I'm like, "But the door is so thick."

00:21:25.530 --> 00:21:27.750
So you're Switzerland in the 1950s

00:21:27.750 --> 00:21:31.410
your big alpine fortress
digging bunkers thing worked.

00:21:31.410 --> 00:21:32.243
And you're like,

00:21:32.243 --> 00:21:35.557
"Let's make everyone have
a bunker in their house

00:21:35.557 --> 00:21:40.380
"so that we can be protected
against nuclear apocalypse."

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:42.390
Okay, cool idea in theory.

00:21:42.390 --> 00:21:46.260
In practice, incredibly
impractical and very expensive.

00:21:46.260 --> 00:21:47.430
So they did what they do

00:21:47.430 --> 00:21:50.220
for just about everything in Switzerland,

00:21:50.220 --> 00:21:51.602
they put it to a vote.

00:21:51.602 --> 00:21:53.400
(gentle ominous music)

00:21:53.400 --> 00:21:57.090
And so in the '60s they
decreed bunkers as a right.

00:21:57.090 --> 00:22:01.080
They actually lined out
exactly how to build bunkers.

00:22:01.080 --> 00:22:03.540
They required everyone to build them

00:22:03.540 --> 00:22:05.850
either retroactively or
in their new buildings.

00:22:05.850 --> 00:22:07.410
And the Swiss government would pay like

00:22:07.410 --> 00:22:10.020
70% of the cost for these bunkers.

00:22:10.020 --> 00:22:12.270
The people would be protected

00:22:12.270 --> 00:22:16.050
using the same strategy
that they've always used,

00:22:16.050 --> 00:22:17.508
digging holes.

00:22:17.508 --> 00:22:18.660
(dramatic pulsing music)

00:22:18.660 --> 00:22:22.020
So I went to the factory of
a company that makes bunkers

00:22:22.020 --> 00:22:25.380
the beds and the dry toilets
and the air ventilation.

00:22:25.380 --> 00:22:27.600
I feel like I'm wandering through the Ikea

00:22:27.600 --> 00:22:30.049
for bomb shelters. (laughs)

00:22:30.049 --> 00:22:31.050
(dramatic pulsing music)

00:22:31.050 --> 00:22:35.220
And perhaps my favorite,
these giant doors.

00:22:35.220 --> 00:22:36.360
Oh my god, these giant doors.

00:22:36.360 --> 00:22:37.830
I've fallen in love with these doors.

00:22:37.830 --> 00:22:38.663
I don't know why.

00:22:38.663 --> 00:22:39.810
They're just large.

00:22:39.810 --> 00:22:42.000
They're really fun to push and pull

00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:43.560
and they're just kind of cartoonish

00:22:43.560 --> 00:22:45.630
because they're so freaking thick.

00:22:45.630 --> 00:22:48.480
Oh my god, look at that door.

00:22:48.480 --> 00:22:50.520
Oh my god, look at this thing.

00:22:50.520 --> 00:22:51.353
Oh yeah, wow.

00:22:53.298 --> 00:22:54.131
- It's nothing-

00:22:54.131 --> 00:22:54.964
- This is nothing special.

00:22:54.964 --> 00:22:56.220
- No. No.
(both laughing)

00:22:56.220 --> 00:22:59.700
- Oh, and they always have
like this yellow wrench

00:22:59.700 --> 00:23:02.310
that I've become very attached
to, the yellow wrench.

00:23:02.310 --> 00:23:04.350
Oh, you see a yellow wrench
and there's a bunker.

00:23:04.350 --> 00:23:06.060
It's like safety or something.

00:23:06.060 --> 00:23:06.893
I don't know.

00:23:06.893 --> 00:23:09.030
Can I buy one of these as a souvenir?

00:23:09.030 --> 00:23:10.213
I've wanted one forever.

00:23:10.213 --> 00:23:13.770
Oh my goodness. I have a yellow wrench.

00:23:13.770 --> 00:23:15.060
I've always wanted one.

00:23:15.060 --> 00:23:16.080
Thank you.

00:23:16.080 --> 00:23:17.940
The bunker industry's been slowing down

00:23:17.940 --> 00:23:20.250
since the end of the Cold
War, for obvious reasons.

00:23:20.250 --> 00:23:22.710
And it's no longer required
by the building code

00:23:22.710 --> 00:23:24.300
for new houses to have a bunker.

00:23:24.300 --> 00:23:26.220
But unfortunately the Swiss bunker

00:23:26.220 --> 00:23:28.801
is now getting a new wave of attention.

00:23:28.801 --> 00:23:30.685
(journalist speaking in foreign language)

00:23:30.685 --> 00:23:34.080
(journalist speaking in foreign language)

00:23:34.080 --> 00:23:36.240
- [Journalist] As the
assault closes in on Kyiv,

00:23:36.240 --> 00:23:37.800
two and a half million civilians

00:23:37.800 --> 00:23:39.720
are suddenly on the front line.

00:23:39.720 --> 00:23:42.750
- Putin's invasion of Ukraine
is changing everything.

00:23:42.750 --> 00:23:44.070
The fear and the risk

00:23:44.070 --> 00:23:47.790
of having to use a bunker
like this is increasing.

00:23:47.790 --> 00:23:49.470
- It's crazy. I mean,
when the war started,

00:23:49.470 --> 00:23:51.870
I've got phone calls and emails daily.

00:23:51.870 --> 00:23:55.590
Interesting, mainly from Germans,
90% of Germans would call.

00:23:55.590 --> 00:23:57.210
In Switzerland We have 11 million

00:23:57.210 --> 00:24:00.150
more than there are people
underground nuclear shelters

00:24:00.150 --> 00:24:01.470
and Germany there's zero.

00:24:01.470 --> 00:24:03.427
So I got calls daily
from people from Germany,

00:24:03.427 --> 00:24:05.105
"Can I rent a room here."

00:24:05.105 --> 00:24:09.022
(speaking in foreign language)

00:24:28.620 --> 00:24:30.540
- People are thinking
about their bunkers again.

00:24:30.540 --> 00:24:32.310
The government is inspecting them

00:24:32.310 --> 00:24:34.307
making sure they have enough.

00:24:34.307 --> 00:24:38.224
(speaking in foreign language)

00:24:39.253 --> 00:24:42.420
I'm in a giant neighborhood bunker

00:24:42.420 --> 00:24:46.740
that is for anyone on this
neighborhood block to come to

00:24:46.740 --> 00:24:48.090
in case of an emergency.

00:24:48.090 --> 00:24:50.220
It's fully decked out as expected,

00:24:50.220 --> 00:24:54.270
and it even has a
full-blown operating room

00:24:54.270 --> 00:24:57.310
and a room for dead bodies.

00:24:57.310 --> 00:24:59.220
(gentle suspenseful music)

00:24:59.220 --> 00:25:00.923
Like that's what that is back there.

00:25:00.923 --> 00:25:03.990
(gentle suspenseful music)

00:25:03.990 --> 00:25:06.840
Putin's invasion of
Ukraine changed everything

00:25:06.840 --> 00:25:08.700
for a lot of places in the world,

00:25:08.700 --> 00:25:09.540
but here in Switzerland

00:25:09.540 --> 00:25:11.250
it didn't only change how people think

00:25:11.250 --> 00:25:13.050
about bunkers and physical safety,

00:25:13.050 --> 00:25:14.850
but it also kicked off a debate

00:25:14.850 --> 00:25:17.760
about the complex topic
of Swiss neutrality.

00:25:17.760 --> 00:25:21.570
- The Swiss government says it is adopting

00:25:21.570 --> 00:25:24.420
the EU sanctions package on Russia.

00:25:24.420 --> 00:25:25.350
That's a huge move.

00:25:25.350 --> 00:25:26.670
- This is Switzerland.

00:25:26.670 --> 00:25:28.920
Who may I remind you did not take a side

00:25:28.920 --> 00:25:30.254
when they came to Hitler.

00:25:30.254 --> 00:25:34.171
(speaking in foreign language)

00:25:36.638 --> 00:25:40.555
(speaking in foreign language)

00:25:41.483 --> 00:25:43.777
- Swiss president, Ignazio Cassis, said,

00:25:43.777 --> 00:25:46.980
"Extraordinary times called
for extraordinary measures."

00:25:46.980 --> 00:25:49.680
- Joining in on sanctions
for a lot of people

00:25:49.680 --> 00:25:51.720
is a massive violation

00:25:51.720 --> 00:25:54.750
of the thing that has kept them neutral

00:25:54.750 --> 00:25:58.010
and peaceful for like 200 years.

00:25:58.010 --> 00:26:01.927
(speaking in foreign language)

00:26:03.030 --> 00:26:04.057
- Several parties saying,

00:26:04.057 --> 00:26:06.690
"well, we should be more flexible."

00:26:06.690 --> 00:26:08.827
More traditional party saying

00:26:08.827 --> 00:26:12.067
"Well, neutrality means
not doing anything,

00:26:12.067 --> 00:26:14.917
"not joining any party,
not helping anything,

00:26:14.917 --> 00:26:17.320
"but rather offer (speaking
in foreign language)."

00:26:18.210 --> 00:26:19.560
I don't how you say...

00:26:19.560 --> 00:26:22.140
(bright twinkly music)

00:26:22.140 --> 00:26:24.420
- Now, we took over the
sanctions from the EU

00:26:24.420 --> 00:26:26.490
which basically makes us a war party.

00:26:26.490 --> 00:26:28.110
Well, I don't like it. I
don't think it's right.

00:26:28.110 --> 00:26:31.170
- If you're from a country
that isn't obsessively neutral

00:26:31.170 --> 00:26:33.390
you're kind of like, "Dude,
you gotta take a stance."

00:26:33.390 --> 00:26:36.780
But here they think differently
about the right side

00:26:36.780 --> 00:26:40.350
and the cost of choosing
a side in conflict

00:26:40.350 --> 00:26:44.070
or more importantly, the
benefit of not choosing a side.

00:26:44.070 --> 00:26:45.210
- I think the Swiss,

00:26:45.210 --> 00:26:48.960
the people themselves want
neutrality which we never know.

00:26:48.960 --> 00:26:51.630
I mean, the majority rules.

00:26:51.630 --> 00:26:52.564
It's democracy.

00:26:52.564 --> 00:26:55.814
(bright twinkly music)

00:26:57.960 --> 00:27:00.090
- Okay, well, that's it.

00:27:00.090 --> 00:27:02.520
That is my journey.

00:27:02.520 --> 00:27:05.340
I have to say, this story left
a bit of an impression on me.

00:27:05.340 --> 00:27:08.310
I came here thinking I
was gonna go hiking around

00:27:08.310 --> 00:27:11.160
and stumble upon some abandoned
bunkers in the forest,

00:27:11.160 --> 00:27:12.360
but as I dug into this,

00:27:12.360 --> 00:27:15.240
I found myself understanding
Switzerland in a new way.

00:27:15.240 --> 00:27:18.300
This place where the people
didn't colonize other countries

00:27:18.300 --> 00:27:21.030
but stayed here digging in their mountains

00:27:21.030 --> 00:27:25.260
so obsessively to defend
their ideas about neutrality.

00:27:25.260 --> 00:27:28.560
A neutrality that is finding new meaning

00:27:28.560 --> 00:27:29.973
in a changing world.

00:27:31.290 --> 00:27:32.719
Thanks for watching.

00:27:32.719 --> 00:27:35.969
(bright twinkly music)

00:27:46.170 --> 00:27:50.910
Hey, so I filmed so much more
than was put into this video.

00:27:50.910 --> 00:27:52.627
Boy, the work has just begun.

00:27:52.627 --> 00:27:53.460
Oh, I'm the drone.

00:27:53.460 --> 00:27:55.172
It's kind of scaring me right now.

00:27:55.172 --> 00:27:56.005
(upbeat music)

00:27:56.005 --> 00:27:58.582
It's old, it's kind of broken,
it's not as good and...

00:27:58.582 --> 00:28:00.330
(metal clinking)

00:28:00.330 --> 00:28:01.440
(upbeat music)

00:28:01.440 --> 00:28:03.932
I used to hear a lot about the American...

00:28:03.932 --> 00:28:05.030
Oh, shit. (beep)

00:28:05.030 --> 00:28:06.750
This is what it takes to get a bunker.

00:28:06.750 --> 00:28:07.890
Oh, (beep)

00:28:07.890 --> 00:28:09.543
Okay, I gotta go find that drone.

00:28:11.040 --> 00:28:12.510
It's almost a travesty.

00:28:12.510 --> 00:28:14.910
So much so that I'm finally done

00:28:14.910 --> 00:28:16.890
not doing behind the scenes.

00:28:16.890 --> 00:28:20.880
I'm gonna start putting a
bunch of BTS up on Patreon.

00:28:20.880 --> 00:28:24.180
Patreon is a place that
I turn to for support

00:28:24.180 --> 00:28:25.710
in a world where I'm trying to do deeper

00:28:25.710 --> 00:28:27.990
more factually correct journalism

00:28:27.990 --> 00:28:29.940
that is expensive and time consuming.

00:28:29.940 --> 00:28:32.460
So over on Patreon I'm
gonna start to publish

00:28:32.460 --> 00:28:34.380
behind the scene vlogs

00:28:34.380 --> 00:28:35.910
or show you how all this stuff is made.

00:28:35.910 --> 00:28:38.250
I'm also gonna publish a full version

00:28:38.250 --> 00:28:41.190
of this tour that I did
through Eric's Bunker.

00:28:41.190 --> 00:28:43.170
It's way longer and way cooler

00:28:43.170 --> 00:28:45.510
than the two seconds I was
able to put in this video.

00:28:45.510 --> 00:28:47.280
And going forward I'll be doing

00:28:47.280 --> 00:28:49.140
behind the scenes stuff from the studio

00:28:49.140 --> 00:28:50.520
and from my other travels

00:28:50.520 --> 00:28:51.930
so that you can see how this is made.

00:28:51.930 --> 00:28:53.670
You've been asking for it for a long time.

00:28:53.670 --> 00:28:56.220
I've been resisting for some reason.

00:28:56.220 --> 00:28:57.330
I'm done resisting.

00:28:57.330 --> 00:29:00.840
Go become a Patreon and help
support independent journalism.

00:29:00.840 --> 00:29:01.980
If you wanna support in other ways,

00:29:01.980 --> 00:29:04.860
there's lots in presets
that are in the description.

00:29:04.860 --> 00:29:08.070
And thank you Switzerland
for another amazing trip.

00:29:08.070 --> 00:29:09.527
I'll see you soon.

00:29:09.527 --> 00:29:12.860
(gentle ominous music)

